WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
MARK MIRCHANDANI: Not sure where
to look for your Google Cloud

00:00:02.583 --> 00:00:03.630
Platform payment details?

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.088
In this video,
we'll cover what you

00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:07.710
need to know about payment
methods, your GCP invoice,

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.050
and where to go to answer
detailed cost questions.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.417
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.430
When you use a GCP
resource, you'll

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.760
need a method to pay for it.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.220
And there's two
ways to do this--

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.020
online or invoiced.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.810
Online, also sometimes
referred to as self-service,

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.150
is where payments are made
online with a credit or debit

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:29.683
card.

00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:31.850
This is the default option
when setting up a billing

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.220
account using Google
Cloud Platform.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.930
Invoiced is where a
request for payment

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.220
is made through an invoice.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.310
And payment is made through
a check or a wire transfer.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.903
This method is sometimes
referred to as offline billing.

00:00:42.903 --> 00:00:45.320
Some customers are eligible
to change their billing method

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.780
to a monthly invoice
billing structure.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.180
Eligibility depends on a
variety of factors, including

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.770
how long your account
has been active,

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.478
the typical amount of
your monthly spend,

00:00:53.478 --> 00:00:54.920
and your country.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.170
An invoice billing account
is much more common

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.270
for larger organizations.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.550
If you have a dedicated
finance or accounting team

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.160
or if you anticipate
a large GCP spend,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.530
you'll want to work with your
GCP sales team or billing

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.110
support to set up an
invoice billing account.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.090
The key thing to remember
is that all customers

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.520
receive a monthly PDF
summarizing their costs

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:14.930
from the previous month.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.120
Customers who are using
the online payment method

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.380
receive a monthly statement.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.630
Customers who have switched
to invoice billing account

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:24.010
receive a PDF invoice, which
is the request for payment.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.462
An invoice for a
particular month

00:01:25.462 --> 00:01:27.170
should be available
by the fifth business

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.580
day of the following month.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:30.410
For example, your
September invoice

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:32.630
will be ready no
later than October 5.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.390
Invoices aren't generated on
weekends or bank holidays.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:37.190
So you should expect
invoices to be

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.140
delayed during those periods.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.090
If you want to receive
invoices by email,

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:43.580
or you want to change
who receives invoices,

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.580
refer to the payments contacts
and notification settings

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.720
managing your payments profile.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.350
Now, before we take a closer
look at the sample invoice,

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.100
the first thing you
need to know is this--

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.280
an invoice essentially
tells you what you owe.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.790
That's about it.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.030
If you want to get a full
picture of your GCP costs

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.070
and answer detailed
cost questions,

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.170
you should refer to the billing
reports in the GCP console.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.680
So when in doubt, remember--
your invoice tells you

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:07.670
what you owe.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:11.220
Billing reports tell you why
and where your cost came from.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.860
Now, let's take a
look at the details

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.990
included in a typical invoice.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.520
Here's a sample invoice.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.900
On the first page,
you can expect

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.340
to find some key
pieces of information.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.645
First off, you can see who
the invoice is addressed to.

00:02:22.645 --> 00:02:24.770
This information would have
been provided to Google

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.170
at the time invoice
billing account was set up.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:29.130
To edit or update
this information,

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:31.470
refer to the payments
profile settings.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.310
Next, you'll find details, such
as the invoice date, payment

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.980
terms, which is usually
full payment within 30 days,

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.450
and the account ID.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.340
The account ID might
be helpful in cases

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.470
where you're inquiring
about specific charges

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.427
on your invoice.

00:02:43.427 --> 00:02:45.260
If you're not able to
resolve your questions

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.098
with the help of your
billing account admin,

00:02:47.098 --> 00:02:49.640
you can request that they submit
a ticket to the Google Cloud

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:50.683
support team.

00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:52.850
Only your billing account
admins can create a ticket

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.410
with billing support.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.630
On the right, you'll
also see the total amount

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.510
owed in a single
currency and a line item

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.100
showing the taxes applied.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.930
All discounts
previously negotiated

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.670
as part of your
Google Cloud agreement

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.190
would have already been
applied to the total.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:08.880
And at the bottom
of the first page,

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.880
you'll find instructions
for paying your invoice

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.520
either by wire
transfer or by check.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.650
In subsequent pages,
you'll see a summary table

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:18.240
with details based on
your GCP consumption.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.180
The first column is the product.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.680
It's fairly self-explanatory.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.920
It refers to the GCP service
that reported the billing data.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.750
Resource type is a
brief description

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.580
of the specific resource
that was used by the service.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.990
For example, a resource type
of line item for Compute Engine

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:35.330
is the charge for static IPs.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.850
Next, is the interval, which
lists the start and end

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.910
dates of resource usage
for that billing cycle.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.370
Usage lists the quantity
of the service used.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.140
You might notice the
unit of consumption

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.360
will differ depending
on the resource type.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.970
For example, a VPN tunnel
under Compute Engine

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.080
will be listed in hours.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.630
And finally, for
each row, you'll

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:56.160
see the calculated
cost under amount.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.970
Note that the calculated cost
includes your discounted rate.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.890
If you want to see a
more detailed breakout

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.050
of your costs, refer
to the billing reports

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.790
in the GCP console.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.710
Let's look at an example
of how resource types

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:08.330
for a specific
product are priced,

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.190
such as for Compute Engine.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:13.670
Charges are based on compute
instances, storage, and network

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:14.720
use.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.420
Virtual machines are
charged on per second basis

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.910
with a one minute minimum usage.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:23.420
Storage is calculated based on
the amount of data you store.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.790
Network cost is calculated
based on the amount of data

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:28.070
transferred between virtual
machine instances that

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:30.830
communicate with each other
and with the internet.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.530
To learn more about how various
resource types are priced,

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:37.160
refer to
cloud.google.com/pricing.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.580
If you need to view previous
invoices or invoices past due,

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.530
you can access them
in the console.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.360
Using the left-hand
navigation, click

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:45.980
Billing to choose
a billing account,

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.960
and then select Invoices.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.990
From this page, you can filter
by all invoices and memos

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.920
or just by open ones.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.680
It's also easy to
create custom filters

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.138
and search so that you can find
the information that you're

00:04:57.138 --> 00:04:58.400
looking for.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.530
Clicking on an item lets
you see the full detail,

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:04.020
such as the invoice number,
amount, and payment due date.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:06.050
In addition, you can
download a PDF version

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:08.030
if you want to share the
invoice between teams

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:12.030
or even download a CSV version,
which makes it easier to parse.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.790
Remember, the invoice
is intentionally

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.350
designed to show you a
summary of what you owe.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.850
Depending on your
specific need, you

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.710
might have additional questions.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.630
Here's a few tips for where
you can get more information.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.620
Get to know your organization's
GCP billing account admins.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.870
There may be more than one
admin in your organization.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:31.170
And working together to plan,
track, and pay for your GCP

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.630
costs will prove
helpful in the long run.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:36.810
If you're looking for detailed
views of your GCP costs,

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.482
refer to the billing
reports in the GCP console.

00:05:39.482 --> 00:05:41.940
If you want to review the price
list for different resource

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.430
types, check out the Google
Cloud pricing website

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.550
or access the
information via the API.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:50.160
For more information about your
invoice or to resolve common

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:55.350
billing issues, check out
cloud.google.com/billing/docs.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.300
That's it for payment
methods and invoices.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.620
Check out the links to
learn more information.

